  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "nm4nd5dmj",
      "node_id": "node-user-data-fetch-cdbb8066",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "User Data Fetch",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": {
            "text": {
              "text": {
                "text": {
                  "text": {
                    "text": "Finds a random behavioral twin from a vector database using CIBIL bucket membership.\n\nThis node retrieves a similar user record (a “behavioral twin”) from a demo user vector database based primarily on the CIBIL score bucket. It first extracts the CIBIL value from the user profile string, converts it to a bucket (e.g., “excellent”, “very_good”, “fair”, “poor”, or “ntc” for no credit history). It then builds a retrieval query that includes the bucket and a numeric range hint (e.g., “cibil_score around 780”) to help the vector database find records with comparable scores. After querying, the node filters candidates strictly by bucket membership and randomly selects one. If no records match, it falls back to a broader query and returns an error message. This approach ensures behavioral similarity while introducing a controlled randomness suitable for simulation or A/B testing.",
                    "lineHeight": 14,
                    "fontSize": 11,
                    "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                  },
                  "lineHeight": 14,
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                },
                "lineHeight": 14,
                "fontSize": 11,
                "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
              },
              "lineHeight": 14,
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
            },
            "lineHeight": 14,
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
          },
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-user-data-fetch-cdbb8066",
        "name": "User Data Fetch",
        "description": "Finds a random behavioral twin from a vector database using CIBIL bucket membership.\n\nThis node retrieves a similar user record (a “behavioral twin”) from a demo user vector database based primarily on the CIBIL score bucket. It first extracts the CIBIL value from the user profile string, converts it to a bucket (e.g., “excellent”, “very_good”, “fair”, “poor”, or “ntc” for no credit history). It then builds a retrieval query that includes the bucket and a numeric range hint (e.g., “cibil_score around 780”) to help the vector database find records with comparable scores. After querying, the node filters candidates strictly by bucket membership and randomly selects one. If no records match, it falls back to a broader query and returns an error message. This approach ensures behavioral similarity while introducing a controlled randomness suitable for simulation or A/B testing.",
