    {
      "id": "i6m4n7xqf",
      "node_id": "node-accept-user-cibil-data-524091fa",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Accept User CIBIL Data",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": {
            "text": "Validates and formats employment, income, dependents, and CIBIL into a pipe‑separated profile string for Credit Health Report Generation.\n\nThis node acts as a validation gate for user financial data. It checks that all four required fields (employment type, income range, number of dependents, and CIBIL score) are present and non‑empty. If any field is missing or contains the string “none”, the node returns an empty string, signaling incomplete data. Otherwise, it formats the values into a standardized pipe‑separated string (Emp: ... | Inc: ... | Dep: ... | CIBIL: ...). This consistent format allows downstream nodes to reliably parse user information without repeated validation logic.",
            "lineHeight": 14,
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
          },
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-accept-user-cibil-data-524091fa",
        "name": "Accept User CIBIL Data",
