    {
      "id": "u1u5v710p",
      "node_id": "node-context-generator-(qwen)-17f7f580",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Text Generate (Qwen)",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": "This node performs text generation using a preloaded Qwen language model, converting an input prompt into a coherent natural language response. The model and its tokenizer are already provided by the wrapper, so the node focuses on preparing inputs and executing generation.\n\nThe prompt is first tokenized and moved to the same device as the model (typically GPU for faster inference). The node then calls the model’s generate method, applying configurable sampling parameters such as temperature (controls randomness), top_p (nucleus sampling), and max_new_tokens (response length). These settings allow fine control over creativity, diversity, and output size.\n\nOnce generation is complete, the output tokens are decoded back into readable text, with special tokens removed. The final result is a clean text string representing the model’s response to the given prompt.",
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-context-generator-(qwen)-17f7f580",
        "name": "Text Generate (Qwen)",
        "description": "This node performs text generation using a preloaded Qwen language model, converting an input prompt into a coherent natural language response. The model and its tokenizer are already provided by the wrapper, so the node focuses on preparing inputs and executing generation.\n\nThe prompt is first tokenized and moved to the same device as the model (typically GPU for faster inference). The node then calls the model’s generate method, applying configurable sampling parameters such as temperature (controls randomness), top_p (nucleus sampling), and max_new_tokens (response length). These settings allow fine control over creativity, diversity, and output size.\n\nOnce generation is complete, the output tokens are decoded back into readable text, with special tokens removed. The final result is a clean text string representing the model’s response to the given prompt.",
        "category": "llm_qwen",
